[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-cac038b7-10c1-4635-87d8-b8fb6efc46e1\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Wed 15 Apr 2026 11:30 - 11:45 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-oceania-iv\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Oceania IV</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Requirements and Modeling 1</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/matteocamilli\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Matteo Camilli</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"cac038b7-10c1-4635-87d8-b8fb6efc46e1\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Can SAT Solvers Keep Up With the Linux Kernel's Feature Model?</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"This paper won an award as a distinguished paper\" class=\"output-badge\"><span class=\"label-primary label\">Distinguished Paper Award</span></span></span><p>The Linux kernel is a highly relevant, yet also highly configurable software system. Kernel developers keep track of this configurability in a feature model, which defines the features of Linux and their dependencies. To support kernel developers in various activities, many (semi-)automated product-line analyses have been proposed over the years. Under the hood, these analyses can often be computed with SAT solvers. Yet, the Linux kernel has constantly been growing in complexity for decades, which increasingly hampers its efficient analysis. At the same time, SAT solvers have been improving in performance for decades, which eases analysis. In this paper, we investigate empirically whether SAT solvers can keep up with the Linux kernel\u2019s feature model. To this end, we analyze historic feature models of Linux with historic SAT solvers from several sources. We find that SAT solvers are generally not able to keep up with Linux. Even the optimal SAT solver is slowing down by 10% every year, meaning that its performance halves every seven years. We conclude that the Linux kernel will become increasingly difficult to analyze if its growth is not counteracted.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SoftVarE-Group/Papers/main/2026/2026-ICSE-Kuiter.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/eliaskuiter\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Elias Kuiter\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/eliaskuiter/eb20ca6e-ff2f-4c03-8f04-b96891e7717c/micro-avatar?1783980327000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Elias Kuiter<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Magdeburg</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Germany</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/ursbenedictbraun\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Urs-Benedict Braun<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Magdeburg</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/thomasthum\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Thomas Th&uuml;m\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/thomasthum/258e8cd9-9326-4d05-b16e-ee2c85f06c13/micro-avatar?1783974929000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Thomas Th\u00FCm<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">TU Braunschweig</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Germany</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/sebastiankrieter2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Sebastian Krieter<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">TU Braunschweig, Germany</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/guntersaake\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Gunter Saake<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of Magdeburg, Germany</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/295/Can-SAT-Solvers-Keep-Up-With-the-Linux-Kernel-s-Feature-Model-\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-cac038b7-10c1-4635-87d8-b8fb6efc46e1').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
